<!--
  Sparkle's update feed for Quill. SUFeedURL (Resources/Info.plist) points
  here via jsDelivr's GitHub CDN mirror (cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/...@master),
  not raw.githubusercontent.com directly — confirmed via a real release
  that raw.githubusercontent.com's Fastly edge cache can serve a stale
  appcast for several minutes after a push, inconsistently across edge
  locations (one geographic edge refreshed almost immediately, another
  hadn't after a full app quit-and-relaunch), which defeats the whole
  point of "push and it's live." jsDelivr has the same problem in
  principle (also CDN-cached, ~7 day default TTL) but supports an
  explicit purge: after pushing this file, hit
  https://purge.jsdelivr.net/gh/imtamiliniyan/quill@master/appcast.xml
  (a plain GET) to force that edge cache to drop the old copy — that GET
  is the step that actually makes a new version visible to the app's
  automatic background check and "Check for Updates…" menu item, same
  as the plain git push used to be with raw.githubusercontent.com.

  Newest <item> goes first. Generate one via scripts/release-appcast.sh
  after scripts/build-app.sh, then paste it in here by hand — reviewed
  before it's pushed, same discipline as the GitHub Releases themselves
  (see .github/workflows/release.yml's `draft: true` comment).

-->
